<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siwana</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Siwana is a town in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, dominated by a hill fort on the edge of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thar-desert">Thar Desert</a>. Held by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chauhan">Chauhans</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jalore">Jalor</a>, the fort was besieged by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alauddin-khalji">Alauddin Khalji</a> in 1308; its commander Sitaladeva was killed and the fort fell before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> army moved on to Jalor. It later passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rathore">Rathores of Marwar</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/siwana.jpg" alt="Siwana" width="320" height="250" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wikiwizardinho · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Haldeshwar_Mahadev_temple.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
